From 33a64947beebfa6056013735a107bc413f37ac57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JU <jusamuel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:43:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): server-first collection plan and data-map
 channel mapping (C5d)

- CollectionPlanBuilder: priority server -> built-in (or given) profile -> default for frameRule,
  cmdGapMs, initDelayMs, initRoutine, PTL_TYPE/roles (when server roles set), action, expect,
  idempotent, tx, parse. Per-item source in CollectionPlan.Sources; missing or invalid server values
  fall back with a warning (no exception).
- Channel mapping from GET /api/core/sync/data-map (scale/offset, PTL_CD filter, unit/range from tag);
  TAG_ID=CH<n> temporary mapping kept when the device has no map rows.
- SyncModels: C5c fields (nullable, old server responses still read), DataChannelMapSync;
  JuProviderApiClient.GetDataMapAsync; Rules/ExpectRule shared with the builder.
- Tests: server-only plan equals built-in plan, virtual GTEC full cycle with server values only
  (init/START/data/STOP/disconnect/reconnect), fallback cases, Java/.NET regex vectors,
  server-side boundary tests (roles-less protocols, unchanged-field skip scope).

